-- `primitives.js` — common CDP primitives (`eval`, `getText`, `captureScreenshot`, `waitFor`)
+- `primitives.js` — common CDP primitives (`eval`, `getText`, `captureScreenshot`, `waitFor`, locators, real input events)
+- `dom.js` — page-side helpers (roles, accessible names, refs, live regions) evaluated inside the target
 - `observation.js` — network and event observation helpers
 
 ## Security
@@ -64,6 +65,16 @@ cdpkit is read-only by default. Never send, post, edit, or mutate state in any a
 - Use `Page.getLayoutMetrics().cssLayoutViewport` and `cssContentSize` for screenshot clips so Retina displays capture correctly.
 - Combine the screenshot with read methods (`getMessages`, `searchMessages`, `getText`, `search`) to answer user questions.
 
+### Chrome
+
+- `chrome.getContext(client)` returns `{ url, title, visibleText, interactables, alerts, screenshot }`. `interactables` is an accessibility-style list of visible controls (`{ ref, role, name, value, checked, disabled, expanded, selector }`); `alerts` surfaces live regions (`role=alert`/`aria-live`) and invalid fields (`aria-invalid`, `:user-invalid`) so validation errors are visible without a screenshot.
+- Every action takes a **locator**: a CSS selector string, a ref from the snapshot (`"@e12"`), or a descriptor such as `{ role: "button", text: "Next" }`, `{ label: "First name" }`, `{ placeholder: "Search" }`. Descriptors are matched against visible elements only unless `visible: false`; add `index` to disambiguate.
+- `click(client, locator)` scrolls into view and dispatches real mouse events via `Input.dispatchMouseEvent`, falling back to `el.click()` when the point is covered (pass `{ js: true }` to force). `type(client, locator, text)` focuses and uses `Input.insertText`, so React-style controlled inputs see trusted events. `select(client, locator, option)` handles native `<select>` and ARIA combobox/listbox widgets. `press(client, "Enter")` sends key combos (`"Control+a"`, `"Escape"`, `"Tab"`).
+- Actions settle by default: they wait until the DOM has been quiet for ~400ms. For explicit transitions prefer `waitForUrl`, `waitForText`, or `waitForElement` over sleeps; `waitForStable` is available on its own.
+- Tabs: `tabs(s)`, `switchTab(s, (t) => t.url.includes(...))`, `newTab(s, url)`, `closeTab(s, targetId)`. `switchTab` rebinds `s.client` to the chosen target.
+- Screenshots: `captureScreenshot(client, { fullPage: true, path })` writes to disk and returns the path instead of a base64 payload; `getContext(client, { screenshotPath })` does the same.
+- Linux is supported: Chrome is discovered on `PATH` (`google-chrome`, `chromium`, …) or via `CDPKIT_CHROME`.
+
 ### Slack
 
 - Prefer the cdpkit helpers; they call the in-app Slack APIs directly. Do not rely on the stale redux cache.
